{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/pulls/5071","id":4755730171,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIdn7C88AAAABG3au-w","html_url":"https://github.com/snissn/gomap/pull/5071","diff_url":"https://github.com/snissn/gomap/pull/5071.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/snissn/gomap/pull/5071.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/issues/5071","number":5071,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Bound TreeDB churn ownership and add retained row-store qualification harnesses","user":{"login":"snissn","id":1981537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODE1Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1981537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn","html_url":"https://github.com/snissn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snissn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Repeated row churn retained obsolete leaf packs, immutable manifest revisions and successful native appender creation history, while deletion retries could outlive manager shutdown. This repairs ownership through the existing manager, recovery roots and GC, and adds the supported lifecycle and mutation-cost harnesses needed to qualify R1.\n\nImplements #5066 and incorporates the reviewed nine-file mutation harness from #5072 under parent #5056, on main `3cfe2ad8`. #5059 mutation-cost acceptance and #5060/#5061 retained evidence remain open after this code lands.\n\n- Cancel and join admitted deletion retries before manager files close; concurrent Close shares completion and errors.\n- Protect current, both selectable fallback roots, prepared publication and held readers while reclaiming obsolete immutable revisions through exact namespace leases and durable quarantine. Revalidate inventory and fresh protection before every batch. GC owns at most 18 child descriptors: 16 selected deletion handles, one scan child or quarantine placeholder, and one temporary link-validation handle.\n- Keep the exact quarantine placeholder open until deletion returns; validate its link before cleanup and before rename overwrites the destination. Failed cleanup joins causes, preserves canonical/rebound evidence and poisons maintenance with ErrRecoveryRequired. Successful cleanup preserves the original error and permits retry.\n- Select each rebuilt current leaf pack's exact physical closure while protected roots retain theirs. Retire successful native registration history only for the exact manager-owned file; ambiguous, failed, unrelated and standalone rewrite records stay protected.\n- Qualify the supported command-WAL lifecycle fixture, persisted options, full-root census and maintenance boundaries. Capability guards refuse unsupported promotion fixtures before construction.\n- Add a generic row-replacement cost sweep: two payload widths 96/4096, request batches 1/32, indexed/unindexed collections and bio/email-city changes. Retained mode uses 4096 rows, 100 requests and five fresh-DB repetitions across 16 cells. Report acknowledgement latency separately from Flush latency and physical sync/WAL counters. Independent validation requires externally frozen source and six exact provenance pins; producer validation remains UNQUALIFIED.\n\nRevision GC completes eligible batches in one explicit call and preserves deletion counts on later failure. Writer and snapshot-admission locks span the call; repeated scans cost O(N²/16). Per-phase footprint admission is not a cumulative I/O or pause quota. No production rotation cap, WAL mode, automatic maintenance policy or on-disk format changes. The persistent value/leaf logs remain storage, separate from redo WAL.\n\nValidation uses Linux185/111, Go1.26.4, GOWORK=off and matching isolated caches:\n\n- Current runtime `cb5b0d7b` at source `8506a498` passes 114 focused test rows normally in 74.603s and under race in 126.954s, plus vet. All TreeDB runtime/test blobs apply unchanged to final candidate `ebe414b6`. Coverage includes R1 mutation 18 process-exit cuts, lifecycle maintenance three process-exit cuts, current/held/prepared/both recovery roots, revision namespace protection, RLIMIT64 with257 revisions, exact quarantine cleanup and manager retry shutdown.\n- Exact `ebe414b6` passes 51 additive test rows normally in 42.459s and under race in 53.255s, plus vet. These cover the reviewed C smoke/corruption harness and current-main shared writer-observer, rewrite-winning-revision, held physical pointer/reopen and accepted command-WAL wait-failure paths.\n- Independent reviews at exact `ebe414b6` find no material integration defect in the 56 changed upstream production inputs or the incorporated C harness. All 1,122 runtime inputs are frozen; C code/test/capture blobs match reviewed `90fa3dc6`. Fresh runtime performance is required rather than inferred from unchanged workload source.\n- Canonical CI inventory remains 14  workflows / 56 members. All 58 Python contract tests pass at `8506`; the 36 affected inventory/impact tests also pass at final `ebe414`. Unchanged contract/headroom checks retain their original source binding.\n- Original focused cleanup `52bc2147`, broader bounded-GC, pack/current/fallback, native creation-history RED/GREEN, packet guards and supported rehearsals remain retained under their actual source identities. The initial sparse-checkout missing-module refusal, broad collections timeout and isolated passing vector test remain preserved.\n\nThe public 32-revision smoke is correctness/cost smoke only. Final landed-source A/C/D will measure reads, mutation cost, repeated maintenance, physical component growth and sampled memory. Logical census is not allocated blocks; sampled heap is not RSS or an exact peak. Finite active/latest-per-lane retention and bounded descriptors do not establish unlimited capacity or latency bounds. The mutation sweep does not claim native partial-setter, metadata-reference update cost, larger-population or concurrent throughput.\n\nAuxiliary M0 timing at original `3182` remains FAIL/INCONCLUSIVE: all 20 samples passed correctness; one unchanged matched main/control experiment also failed the unchanged noise rule with all 40 correctness samples passing. [Original disposition and evidence](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/pull/5071#issuecomment-6015235219) remain preserved. The user explicitly approved the auxiliary M0 red/inconclusive merge exception on 2026-10-06. This waives only that timing signal; required current-head CI, code/review gates and fresh A/C/D outcome acceptance still apply. No threshold, sample count, outlier or original result changed.\n\nRefs #5066, #5059, #5060, #5061, #5056. Does not close retained qualification or parent gates. External rewrite owner #5037 retains its scope.\n","created_at":"2026-10-06T07:43:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T18:28:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"89fd901c3dec77dc9cb07a1dbfc060a7026f52a5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/pulls/5071/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/pulls/5071/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/issues/5071/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snissn/gomap/statuses/ebe414b6d6a22a7f616c108157a01f8ed109e7cc